============================================================
DECISION RECORD — t_g_m2 greeting generation (2026-09-05)
============================================================

ATTEMPT 1 — scripts/generate-cloned-greeting.ts against the ElevenLabs REST API,
credentials loaded from /root/.claude/.env.production via a scratch env file
(node --env-file), never sourced into this shell and never printed.

  Key names read (values never printed, never committed):
    ELEVENLABS_API_KEY
    ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID

  POST https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/text-to-speech/{ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID}
  →  HTTP 400 Bad Request
  →  code "invalid_api_key" / status "api_key_id_used_as_api_key"

  The failure is the CREDENTIAL, not the voice id: authentication is rejected
  before the voice is ever resolved. The stored value does begin with 'sk_' but
  is a key *ID*, which ElevenLabs distinguishes from a key. Both ELEVENLABS_*
  pairs in .env.production are byte-identical (verified with `sort -u | wc -l`
  → 1), so there is no second credential to try. No asset was written; the
  script exits non-zero rather than falling back to anything fabricated.

  This corroborates the note that was already sitting in MiniVicBot.tsx before
  this change: "A true ElevenLabs voice-clone of Vikram requires a valid
  ElevenLabs `sk_` key (none is provisioned; the stored value is a key *ID*)".

